      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Please stop taking those potassium pills immediately; taking potassium supplements when you have kidney disease is extremely dangerous. Your kidneys are already struggling to manage electrolytes, and adding high doses of potassium could lead to a life-threatening condition called hyperkalemia. You must consult your nephrologist or a healthcare provider who is familiar with your specific kidney function before attempting any changes to your medication or diet.",
