      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The risk is still too high, even with half a pill, because your kidneys are not filtering properly. Any extra potassium can build up quickly and become toxic to your heart. Instead of self-medicating, try drinking plenty of water and eat potassium-rich foods that are safe for your specific dietary plan, like certain approved fruits. Call your doctor's nurse line today to discuss your immediate symptoms.",
      "source": "target",
